Track 1: Switchblade Steam-Engine Leaves the Pier
- Story & Context: At 4:00 AM in the misty canal docks of Bang Pa-In, Granny Somchai cut the brake lines of a regional cargo barge while blowing a deafening warning call through her rusted silver whistle. The distorted surf guitar kicked in just as the diesel engine seized, sending a wave of wake-mud directly into the security office window. The youth on the riverbank cheered as the boat drifted away, setting off the first true Silt-Spit riot. As the alarm bells rang out, Somchai screamed into her carbon mic, "You can't buy the water when the water burns back!"
