Track 2: Bang Khen Junction Slam-Shift
- Story & Context: Under the iron girders of the abandoned Bang Khen rail depot, seventeen-year-old rhythm guitarist Lek confessed his fear of taking over his family's floating produce stall to the Granny-Jacks. Instead of sympathy, Somchai handed him an overdriven Stratocaster wired straight into a diesel generator and told him to play until his fingers bled on the steel fretboard. The track captures the exact moment his fear turned into pure, frantic speed-picking, accompanied by a relentless, screeching whistle that echoed down the empty train tracks. He spat onto the hot vacuum tubes and howled, "Track four is dead and I'm taking the switch!"
